Package: researchAgentR
Title: LLM Agents for Research, Built from First Principles in R
Version: 0.1.5
Authors@R:
    person("Hudson", "Golino", , "hfg9s@virginia.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1601-1447"))
Description: Build, trace, evaluate and optimize large language model agents
    for research, in plain R. Provides one client for many model providers
    (OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions, the OpenAI Responses API and the
    Anthropic Messages API, covering Groq, OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini,
    Ollama and any compatible endpoint), tools defined from R functions, a
    short and readable agent loop with budgets and explicit stop reasons, an
    episode ledger with token, cost and latency for every step, context
    management, memory and retrieval, research tools (OpenAlex, Crossref,
    Semantic Scholar, Europe PMC, arXiv, Unpaywall, NIH RePORTER, NSF,
    Grants.gov, web search), citation and claim verification, multi-agent
    patterns, a Model Context Protocol client, an evaluation harness with
    pass@k, pass^k, cost per success and paired bootstrap comparisons, and
    tools for creating skills, learning a writing style and reviewing
    manuscripts.
